---
globs: scripts/expressions/**
alwaysApply: false
---
Expressions are a special function in Accela that compile into javascript run in HTML. 
- they have a special syntax for input variables: expression.getValue(variableName)
- there are form variables and field variables

Form Variables represent the entire form and have the following capabilities

.message = "A Message"; - this prints HTML at the top of the form
.blockSubmit = true/false; - this prevents or allows the form to be submitted

Field variables
.value - gets the value of the field.
.hidden = true/false; - controls the display of the field
.readOnly = true/false; - set the field to read only
.message = "A message"; - displays a message next to the form field

When getting an ASI form (custom form), we use this syntax: var thisForm = expression.getValue("ASI::FORM");

When getting an ASI field (custom field), we use this syntax: expression.getValue("ASI::SUBGROUP NAME::Field Name");

To complete the actions, we must do a .setReturn(variable) to set the property of the form or field

We can also add HTML controls to the page to for styling. For example:

var fieldStyle = "color: white;background-color: #f44336;margin: 10px 0px;padding:12px;word-break: break-all; word-wrap: break-word;white-space: pre-wrap;";
var fieldMessage = "To verify that you're deleting the correct billing cycle, enter the Billing Parameters Record ID. This action cannot be undone.";
var fieldStyledMessage = "<div style='" + fieldStyle + "'>" + fieldMessage + "</div>"

variable2.message = fieldStyledMessage;
expression.setReturn(variable2);

Here's a full example of an expression:

var servProvCode = expression.getValue("$$servProvCode$$").value;
var thisCapId = expression.getValue("CAP::capModel*altID").value;
var variable0 = expression.getValue("WORKFLOW::dispTaskName");
var variable1 = expression.getValue("WORKFLOW::taskItem*disposition");
var variable2 = expression.getValue("TSI::UNDO BILLINGS::Confirm");
var variable3 = expression.getValue("WORKFLOW::FORM");


var totalRowCount = expression.getTotalRowCount();



if (variable0.value != null && variable0.value.equals(String("Invoice Processing")) && variable1.value != null && variable1.value.equals(String("Execute Batch - Undo Billings"))) {

    var fieldStyle = "color: white;background-color: #f44336;margin: 10px 0px;padding:12px;word-break: break-all; word-wrap: break-word;white-space: pre-wrap;";
    var fieldMessage = "To verify that you're deleting the correct billing cycle, enter the Billing Parameters Record ID. This action cannot be undone.";
    var fieldStyledMessage = "<div style='" + fieldStyle + "'>" + fieldMessage + "</div>"

    variable2.hidden = false;
    variable2.required = true;
    variable2.message = fieldStyledMessage;
    expression.setReturn(variable2);

    var formStyle = "color: white;background-color: #f44336;margin: 10px 0px;padding:12px; width:80%;";
    var formMessage = "<h3>Please complete the confirmation below to proceed with rolling back billings.</h3>";
    formMessage += "<p style='font-size: 16px;'>This action will only delete billing records that have not been finalized. This cannot be undone.</p>";

    var formStyledMessage = "<div style='" + formStyle + "'>" + formMessage + "</div>"
    variable3.message = formStyledMessage;
    expression.setReturn(variable3);

    if (variable2.value != thisCapId) {
        variable3.blockSubmit = true;
        expression.setReturn(variable3);
    }

} else {
    variable2.hidden = true;
    expression.setReturn(variable2);
    variable2.required = false;
    expression.setReturn(variable2);
}

